  "visual_observations": {
    "full427": "All learned methods remove severe noise but omit most fine canopy suspension lines/ribbing visible in exact synthetic GT. Major building/window edges are retained; clouds are smoother than GT. Both new heads are close to one another; no decisive spatial-access advantage is apparent.",
    "known": "Both new heads retain major plate/diagonal edges and the thin pale strand, with smooth dark surfaces. In the 7D chart crop both retain a small isolated bright point and have smooth fields. RawNIND has more uneven edge color/texture in that selected chart crop; this is not a broad camera-superiority claim. Global and spatial outputs look very close.",
    "unseen": "The apple crop is mostly a smooth reddish-brown field in all methods. The second scene retains the broad cream/red boundaries in all methods with residual fine texture varying slightly. No decisive global/spatial detail or color advantage is apparent in these two cases.",
    "gfx": "Both new heads yield smooth sky and retain major building edges and fence diamonds. Fine foliage remains smoothed relative to the independent sharper ISO100 capture. Global/spatial look very similar; no clear fine-detail advantage. RawNIND has stronger uneven/periodic fence texture in this crop. ISO100 differs in aperture/time/moving subjects and is not exact GT; no GFX scoring or broad-superiority claim.",
    "analytic": "Both heads largely suppress the dark8px sinusoidal carrier visible in analytic GT. The brighter16px low-contrast carrier is faintly visible in both, with no decisive spatial advantage. The flat appears smooth. This is a visual observation; signed gains, RMS and all ADC cases remain unread until full native closure.",
    "hue": "Gray and yellow-orange are mostly smooth in both new heads. The saturated magenta field has less visible blotchy modulation in both new heads than V63. Global/spatial are close to each other. No clear new spatial-head color defect appears in these three selected fields; the additional fixed palettes remain required. No numerical bias values have been read.",
    "highlights": "Both new heads and V63 still flatten much of the blue sign interior relative to the independent ISO100 capture. Bright platform bars remain soft with a green/yellow cast. Global/spatial differ only subtly; neither clearly resolves highlight detail. ISO100 AHD differs in capture/aperture/time and is not exact GT; no pixelwise capture score or causal attribution.",
    "hue-extra": "Both new heads smooth bright pale orange/magenta more consistently than V63 in these selected fields. Dark saturated fields are mostly smooth. Global and spatial look close; no clear new spatial-head color defect is apparent in these four fixed palettes."
  },
